  "title": "YouTube's Monetization Requirements for Creators",
  "summary": "YouTube is introducing stricter requirements for creators to earn money through its Partner Program, requiring at least 8,000 watch hours or 20 million Shorts views in the last 90 days, as of February 1, 2027. This reflects a significant increase in the difficulty for creators to monetize their content.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "YouTube requires creators to meet at least 8,000 watch hours over the past year or 20 million Shorts views in the last 90 days.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The new requirements are set to take effect starting February 1, 2027.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "This change is part of broader efforts to increase ad revenue and improve monetization opportunities for creators.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
